course: dictionary
lesson: 12658
title: Formal words: spreading ideas
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Disseminate is a formal word, so you will meet it in serious writing and exams. It means to spread something widely, so that many people get it. Think of it as scattering news, facts or ideas far and wide.
explain: «The school disseminated the news about sports day to every class.» Every class heard the news, so disseminated must mean spread to many people. Check your meaning by swapping in spread: "The school spread the news to every class" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: In science, disseminate can mean scatter, like seeds or a disease. «Dandelion seeds are disseminated by the wind.» The wind carries the seeds far and wide, so they reach many places. Look for clue words like widely, far and wide, or many people.
fact: Disseminate means to spread something widely, to many people or places.
fact: Disseminate is a verb. You can also write disseminates, disseminated or disseminating.
fact: «Disseminate information» means to spread facts so that many people can learn them.
fact: «Widely disseminated» means spread far and wide.
fact: False news can be disseminated very quickly online, so check a story before you share it.
exercise: «The scientists disseminated their results in a journal.» What does disseminated mean? | Lost them | *Spread widely to many people | Hid carefully | Argued about them
exercise: «Dandelion seeds are disseminated by the wind.» What does disseminated mean here? | *Scattered far and wide | Frozen solid | Burned to ash | Counted one by one
exercise: Which phrase means to spread facts so many people can learn them? | Ignore information | Hide information | *Disseminate information | Forget information
test: «Before you share a story online, check it, because false news can be disseminated in minutes.» What does disseminated mean here? | *Spread quickly to many people | Turned into a poem | Tested in a laboratory | Carefully hidden
test: Which word is closest in meaning to disseminate? | *Spread | Whisper quietly | Cancel | Shrink
exam: «Early Christians disseminated their message across the Roman world.» Which word best explains disseminated? | Painted on walls | Locked away | *Spread widely | Argued about
